  anlam='“Dalagan” is the name for stinging nettle in some parts of Anatolia. The “çift dalagan” needle lace (oya) made in Denizli depicts two nettle leaves; the leaves symbolise woman and man. If the two leaves are worked in the same colour they announce love; if in different colours, discord [1]. In Anatolia, oyas were a way of saying what could not be said in words: the same study reports that the “elma çiçeği” (apple blossom) oya, worked in shades of pink and white, expressed youth, health and engagement, and that brides expecting a baby announced the good news with this oya [1].',
